 cipher encrypts block by block in a loop, which is ECB mode: identical plaintext blocks give identical ciphertext blocks. Use cipher.NewGCM with a random nonce.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/cipher#NewGCM](https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/cipher#NewGCM)\n","text":"An AES block cipher encrypts block by block in a loop, which is ECB mode: identical plaintext blocks give identical ciphertext blocks. Use cipher.NewGCM with a random nonce."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.ecb-mode","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.ecb-mode","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.ecb-mode"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An encryption, MAC or token-signing key is a constant in the source code. Anyone with the code can decrypt data or forge signatures and tokens. Load keys from a secrets manager or the environment."},"help":{"markdown":"An encryption, MAC or token-signing key is a constant in the source code. Anyone with the code can decrypt data or forge signatures and tokens. Load keys from a secrets manager or the environment.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/321.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/321.html)\n","text":"An encryption, MAC or token-signing key is a constant in the source code. Anyone with the code can decrypt data or forge signatures and tokens. Load keys from a secrets manager or the environment."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.hardcoded-key","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.hardcoded-key","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-321: Use of Hard-coded Cryptographic Key","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.hardcoded-key"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A token, password, key, salt or nonce is generated with math/rand, whose output is predictable. Use crypto/rand (rand.Read, rand.Text)."},"help":{"markdown":"A token, password, key, salt or nonce is generated with math/rand, whose output is predictable. Use crypto/rand (rand.Read, rand.Text).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/rand](https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/rand)\n","text":"A token, password, key, salt or nonce is generated with math/rand, whose output is predictable. Use crypto/rand (rand.Read, rand.Text)."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.insecure-random-secret","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.insecure-random-secret","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-338: Use of Cryptographically Weak Pseudo-Random Number Generator (PRNG)","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.insecure-random-secret"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The RSA key is shorter than 2048 bits and can be factored with practical effort. Generate at least 3072 bits (2048 is the minimum accepted today), or use an elliptic-curve key."},"help":{"markdown":"The RSA key is shorter than 2048 bits and can be factored with practical effort. Generate at least 3072 bits (2048 is the minimum accepted today), or use an elliptic-curve key.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/rsa#GenerateKey](https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/rsa#GenerateKey)\n","text":"The RSA key is shorter than 2048 bits and can be factored with practical effort. Generate at least 3072 bits (2048 is the minimum accepted today), or use an elliptic-curve key."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.small-rsa-key","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.small-rsa-key","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-326: Inadequate Encryption Strength","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.small-rsa-key"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The IV or GCM nonce is a constant. Reusing an IV with the same key reveals relations between messages and breaks CTR and GCM completely. Fill the IV or nonce from crypto/rand for every message."},"help":{"markdown":"The IV or GCM nonce is a constant. Reusing an IV with the same key reveals relations between messages and breaks CTR and GCM completely. Fill the IV or nonce from crypto/rand for every message.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/cipher](https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/cipher)\n","text":"The IV or GCM nonce is a constant. Reusing an IV with the same key reveals relations between messages and breaks CTR and GCM completely. Fill the IV or nonce from crypto/rand for every message."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.static-iv","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.static-iv","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-323: Reusing a Nonce, Key Pair in Encryption","CWE-329: Generation of Predictable IV with CBC Mode","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.static-iv"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A broken or obsolete cipher (DES, 3DES, RC4, Blowfish, CAST5) is used. Use crypto/aes with GCM, or golang.org/x/crypto/chacha20poly1305."},"help":{"markdown":"A broken or obsolete cipher (DES, 3DES, RC4, Blowfish, CAST5) is used. Use crypto/aes with GCM, or golang.org/x/crypto/chacha20poly1305.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/des](https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/des)\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/rc4](https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/rc4)\n","text":"A broken or obsolete cipher (DES, 3DES, RC4, Blowfish, CAST5) is used. Use crypto/aes with GCM, or golang.org/x/crypto/chacha20poly1305."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.weak-cipher","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.weak-cipher","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.weak-cipher"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"MD5 or SHA-1 is used. Both have practical collision attacks and must not protect integrity, signatures or passwords; use crypto/sha256 or better (and argon2 or bcrypt for passwords)."},"help":{"markdown":"MD5 or SHA-1 is used. Both have practical collision attacks and must not protect integrity, signatures or passwords; use crypto/sha256 or better (and argon2 or bcrypt for passwords).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/md5](https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/md5)\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/sha1](https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/sha1)\n","text":"MD5 or SHA-1 is used. Both have practical collision attacks and must not protect integrity, signatures or passwords; use crypto/sha256 or better (and argon2 or bcrypt for passwords)."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.weak-hash","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.weak-hash","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-328: Use of Weak Hash","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.weak-hash"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The TLS configuration allows SSL 3.0, TLS 1.0 or TLS 1.1, which have known attacks and are deprecated (RFC 8996). Set MinVersion to tls.VersionTLS12 or tls.VersionTLS13."},"help":{"markdown":"The TLS configuration allows SSL 3.0, TLS 1.0 or TLS 1.1, which have known attacks and are deprecated (RFC 8996). Set MinVersion to tls.VersionTLS12 or tls.VersionTLS13.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/tls#Config](https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/tls#Config)\n - [https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8996](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8996)\n","text":"The TLS configuration allows SSL 3.0, TLS 1.0 or TLS 1.1, which have known attacks and are deprecated (RFC 8996). Set MinVersion to tls.VersionTLS12 or tls.VersionTLS13."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.weak-tls-version","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.weak-tls-version","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.go.weak-tls-version"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The cipher runs in ECB mode (\"AES\" alone defaults to AES/ECB/PKCS5Padding), which encrypts identical blocks identically and leaks patterns. Use AES/GCM/NoPadding with a random IV."},"help":{"markdown":"The cipher runs in ECB mode (\"AES\" alone defaults to AES/ECB/PKCS5Padding), which encrypts identical blocks identically and leaks patterns. Use AES/GCM/NoPadding with a random IV.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/specs/security/standard-names.html#cipher-algorithm-modes](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/specs/security/standard-names.html#cipher-algorithm-modes)\n","text":"The cipher runs in ECB mode (\"AES\" alone defaults to AES/ECB/PKCS5Padding), which encrypts identical blocks identically and leaks patterns. Use AES/GCM/NoPadding with a random IV."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.ecb-mode","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.ecb-mode","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.ecb-mode"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A secret key is built from a constant in the source code. Anyone with the code can decrypt data or forge MACs and tokens. Load keys from a key store or secrets manager."},"help":{"markdown":"A secret key is built from a constant in the source code. Anyone with the code can decrypt data or forge MACs and tokens. Load keys from a key store or secrets manager.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/321.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/321.html)\n","text":"A secret key is built from a constant in the source code. Anyone with the code can decrypt data or forge MACs and tokens. Load keys from a key store or secrets manager."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.hardcoded-key","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.hardcoded-key","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-321: Use of Hard-coded Cryptographic Key","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.hardcoded-key"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A token, password, key, salt or nonce is generated with java.util.Random or Math.random(), whose output is predictable. Use java.security.SecureRandom."},"help":{"markdown":"A token, password, key, salt or nonce is generated with java.util.Random or Math.random(), whose output is predictable. Use java.security.SecureRandom.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/security/SecureRandom.html](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/security/SecureRandom.html)\n","text":"A token, password, key, salt or nonce is generated with java.util.Random or Math.random(), whose output is predictable. Use java.security.SecureRandom."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.insecure-random-secret","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.insecure-random-secret","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-338: Use of Cryptographically Weak Pseudo-Random Number Generator (PRNG)","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.insecure-random-secret"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The RSA key pair generator is initialised with fewer than 2048 bits; such keys can be factored with practical effort. Use at least 3072 bits (2048 is the minimum accepted today), or an elliptic-curve key."},"help":{"markdown":"The RSA key pair generator is initialised with fewer than 2048 bits; such keys can be factored with practical effort. Use at least 3072 bits (2048 is the minimum accepted today), or an elliptic-curve key.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/security/KeyPairGenerator.html](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/security/KeyPairGenerator.html)\n","text":"The RSA key pair generator is initialised with fewer than 2048 bits; such keys can be factored with practical effort. Use at least 3072 bits (2048 is the minimum accepted today), or an elliptic-curve key."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.small-rsa-key","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.small-rsa-key","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-326: Inadequate Encryption Strength","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.small-rsa-key"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The IV or GCM nonce is a constant. Reusing an IV with the same key reveals relations between messages and breaks GCM completely. Fill the IV from SecureRandom for every message."},"help":{"markdown":"The IV or GCM nonce is a constant. Reusing an IV with the same key reveals relations between messages and breaks GCM completely. Fill the IV from SecureRandom for every message.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/javax/crypto/spec/IvParameterSpec.html](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/javax/crypto/spec/IvParameterSpec.html)\n","text":"The IV or GCM nonce is a constant. Reusing an IV with the same key reveals relations between messages and breaks GCM completely. Fill the IV from SecureRandom for every message."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.static-iv","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.static-iv","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-323: Reusing a Nonce, Key Pair in Encryption","CWE-329: Generation of Predictable IV with CBC Mode","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.static-iv"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"TLS certificate or host name verification is disabled (a trust manager that accepts every certificate, a host name verifier that accepts every name, or an SSL/TLS 1.0/1.1 context). Any network attacker can then impersonate the server. Use the default trust manager and host name verification."},"help":{"markdown":"TLS certificate or host name verification is disabled (a trust manager that accepts every certificate, a host name verifier that accepts every name, or an SSL/TLS 1.0/1.1 context). Any network attacker can then impersonate the server. Use the default trust manager and host name verification.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Transport_Layer_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Transport_Layer_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n","text":"TLS certificate or host name verification is disabled (a trust manager that accepts every certificate, a host name verifier that accepts every name, or an SSL/TLS 1.0/1.1 context). Any network attacker can then impersonate the server. Use the default trust manager and host name verification."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.tls-verification-disabled","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.tls-verification-disabled","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-295: Improper Certificate Validation","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.tls-verification-disabled"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A broken or obsolete cipher (DES, 3DES, RC4, RC2, Blowfish) is requested from the JCA. Use AES/GCM/NoPadding with a random 12-byte IV."},"help":{"markdown":"A broken or obsolete cipher (DES, 3DES, RC4, RC2, Blowfish) is requested from the JCA. Use AES/GCM/NoPadding with a random 12-byte IV.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/specs/security/standard-names.html#cipher-algorithm-names](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/specs/security/standard-names.html#cipher-algorithm-names)\n","text":"A broken or obsolete cipher (DES, 3DES, RC4, RC2, Blowfish) is requested from the JCA. Use AES/GCM/NoPadding with a random 12-byte IV."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.weak-cipher","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.weak-cipher","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.weak-cipher"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"MD2, MD4, MD5 or SHA-1 is used through a helper library. These hashes have practical collision attacks and must not protect integrity, signatures or passwords; use SHA-256 or better."},"help":{"markdown":"MD2, MD4, MD5 or SHA-1 is used through a helper library. These hashes have practical collision attacks and must not protect integrity, signatures or passwords; use SHA-256 or better.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-codec/apidocs/org/apache/commons/codec/digest/DigestUtils.html](https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-codec/apidocs/org/apache/commons/codec/digest/DigestUtils.html)\n","text":"MD2, MD4, MD5 or SHA-1 is used through a helper library. These hashes have practical collision attacks and must not protect integrity, signatures or passwords; use SHA-256 or better."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.weak-hash","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.weak-hash","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-328: Use of Weak Hash","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.java.weak-hash"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"ECB mode encrypts identical plaintext blocks to identical ciphertext blocks, so patterns in the data stay visible. Use aes-256-gcm with a random IV."},"help":{"markdown":"ECB mode encrypts identical plaintext blocks to identical ciphertext blocks, so patterns in the data stay visible. Use aes-256-gcm with a random IV.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#cryptocreatecipherivalgorithm-key-iv-options](https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#cryptocreatecipherivalgorithm-key-iv-options)\n","text":"ECB mode encrypts identical plaintext blocks to identical ciphertext blocks, so patterns in the data stay visible. Use aes-256-gcm with a random IV."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.ecb-mode","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.ecb-mode","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.ecb-mode"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An encryption, MAC or token-signing key is a constant in the source code. Anyone with the code can decrypt data or forge signatures and tokens. Load keys from a secrets manager or the environment."},"help":{"markdown":"An encryption, MAC or token-signing key is a constant in the source code. Anyone with the code can decrypt data or forge signatures and tokens. Load keys from a secrets manager or the environment.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/321.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/321.html)\n","text":"An encryption, MAC or token-signing key is a constant in the source code. Anyone with the code can decrypt data or forge signatures and tokens. Load keys from a secrets manager or the environment."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.hardcoded-key","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.hardcoded-key","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-321: Use of Hard-coded Cryptographic Key","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.hardcoded-key"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A token, password, key, salt or nonce is generated with Math.random(), whose output is predictable. Use crypto.randomBytes, crypto.randomUUID or crypto.getRandomValues."},"help":{"markdown":"A token, password, key, salt or nonce is generated with Math.random(), whose output is predictable. Use crypto.randomBytes, crypto.randomUUID or crypto.getRandomValues.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Math/random](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Math/random)\n","text":"A token, password, key, salt or nonce is generated with Math.random(), whose output is predictable. Use crypto.randomBytes, crypto.randomUUID or crypto.getRandomValues."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.insecure-random-secret","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.insecure-random-secret","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-338: Use of Cryptographically Weak Pseudo-Random Number Generator (PRNG)","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.insecure-random-secret"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The RSA key is shorter than 2048 bits and can be factored with practical effort. Use a modulusLength of at least 3072 (2048 is the minimum accepted today), or an elliptic-curve key."},"help":{"markdown":"The RSA key is shorter than 2048 bits and can be factored with practical effort. Use a modulusLength of at least 3072 (2048 is the minimum accepted today), or an elliptic-curve key.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#cryptogeneratekeypairtype-options-callback](https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#cryptogeneratekeypairtype-options-callback)\n","text":"The RSA key is shorter than 2048 bits and can be factored with practical effort. Use a modulusLength of at least 3072 (2048 is the minimum accepted today), or an elliptic-curve key."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.small-rsa-key","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.small-rsa-key","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-326: Inadequate Encryption Strength","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.small-rsa-key"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The IV is a constant (a string literal or a zero-filled buffer). Reusing an IV with the same key reveals relations between messages and breaks CTR and GCM completely. Use crypto.randomBytes for every message."},"help":{"markdown":"The IV is a constant (a string literal or a zero-filled buffer). Reusing an IV with the same key reveals relations between messages and breaks CTR and GCM completely. Use crypto.randomBytes for every message.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#cryptocreatecipherivalgorithm-key-iv-options](https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#cryptocreatecipherivalgorithm-key-iv-options)\n","text":"The IV is a constant (a string literal or a zero-filled buffer). Reusing an IV with the same key reveals relations between messages and breaks CTR and GCM completely. Use crypto.randomBytes for every message."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.static-iv","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.static-iv","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-323: Reusing a Nonce, Key Pair in Encryption","CWE-329: Generation of Predictable IV with CBC Mode","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.static-iv"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"checkServerIdentity is replaced by a function that accepts every certificate, so host names are not checked and any certificate for any domain is accepted. Remove the override."},"help":{"markdown":"checkServerIdentity is replaced by a function that accepts every certificate, so host names are not checked and any certificate for any domain is accepted. Remove the override.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://nodejs.org/api/tls.html#tlscheckserveridentityhostname-cert](https://nodejs.org/api/tls.html#tlscheckserveridentityhostname-cert)\n","text":"checkServerIdentity is replaced by a function that accepts every certificate, so host names are not checked and any certificate for any domain is accepted. Remove the override."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.tls-verification-disabled","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.tls-verification-disabled","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-297: Improper Validation of Certificate with Host Mismatch","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.tls-verification-disabled"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A broken or obsolete cipher (DES, 3DES, RC4, RC2, Blowfish, CAST) is used, or crypto.createCipher, which derives the key with MD5 and uses no IV. Use crypto.createCipheriv with aes-256-gcm and a random IV."},"help":{"markdown":"A broken or obsolete cipher (DES, 3DES, RC4, RC2, Blowfish, CAST) is used, or crypto.createCipher, which derives the key with MD5 and uses no IV. Use crypto.createCipheriv with aes-256-gcm and a random IV.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#cryptocreatecipherivalgorithm-key-iv-options](https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#cryptocreatecipherivalgorithm-key-iv-options)\n","text":"A broken or obsolete cipher (DES, 3DES, RC4, RC2, Blowfish, CAST) is used, or crypto.createCipher, which derives the key with MD5 and uses no IV. Use crypto.createCipheriv with aes-256-gcm and a random IV."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.weak-cipher","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.weak-cipher","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.weak-cipher"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"MD5 or SHA-1 is used. Both have practical collision attacks and must not protect integrity, signatures or passwords; use SHA-256 or better (and scrypt or Argon2 for passwords)."},"help":{"markdown":"MD5 or SHA-1 is used. Both have practical collision attacks and must not protect integrity, signatures or passwords; use SHA-256 or better (and scrypt or Argon2 for passwords).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#cryptocreatehashalgorithm-options](https://nodejs.org/api/crypto.html#cryptocreatehashalgorithm-options)\n","text":"MD5 or SHA-1 is used. Both have practical collision attacks and must not protect integrity, signatures or passwords; use SHA-256 or better (and scrypt or Argon2 for passwords)."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.weak-hash","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.weak-hash","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-328: Use of Weak Hash","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.javascript.weak-hash"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"ECB mode encrypts identical plaintext blocks to identical ciphertext blocks, so patterns in the data stay visible and blocks can be reordered. Use an authenticated mode (AES-GCM) with a random nonce."},"help":{"markdown":"ECB mode encrypts identical plaintext blocks to identical ciphertext blocks, so patterns in the data stay visible and blocks can be reordered. Use an authenticated mode (AES-GCM) with a random nonce.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cryptography.io/en/latest/hazmat/primitives/symmetric-encryption/#cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers.modes.ECB](https://cryptography.io/en/latest/hazmat/primitives/symmetric-encryption/#cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers.modes.ECB)\n","text":"ECB mode encrypts identical plaintext blocks to identical ciphertext blocks, so patterns in the data stay visible and blocks can be reordered. Use an authenticated mode (AES-GCM) with a random nonce."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.ecb-mode","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.ecb-mode","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.ecb-mode"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An encryption, MAC or token-signing key is a constant in the source code. Anyone with the code can decrypt data or forge signatures and tokens, and the key cannot be rotated without a release. Load keys from a secrets manager or the environment."},"help":{"markdown":"An encryption, MAC or token-signing key is a constant in the source code. Anyone with the code can decrypt data or forge signatures and tokens, and the key cannot be rotated without a release. Load keys from a secrets manager or the environment.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/321.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/321.html)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Key_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Key_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n","text":"An encryption, MAC or token-signing key is a constant in the source code. Anyone with the code can decrypt data or forge signatures and tokens, and the key cannot be rotated without a release. Load keys from a secrets manager or the environment."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.hardcoded-key","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.hardcoded-key","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-321: Use of Hard-coded Cryptographic Key","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.hardcoded-key"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A token, password, key, salt or nonce is generated with the random module, whose output is predictable (Mersenne Twister). Use the secrets module (secrets.token_urlsafe, secrets.token_bytes) or os.urandom."},"help":{"markdown":"A token, password, key, salt or nonce is generated with the random module, whose output is predictable (Mersenne Twister). Use the secrets module (secrets.token_urlsafe, secrets.token_bytes) or os.urandom.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://docs.python.org/3/library/random.html](https://docs.python.org/3/library/random.html)\n - [https://docs.python.org/3/library/secrets.html](https://docs.python.org/3/library/secrets.html)\n","text":"A token, password, key, salt or nonce is generated with the random module, whose output is predictable (Mersenne Twister). Use the secrets module (secrets.token_urlsafe, secrets.token_bytes) or os.urandom."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.insecure-random-secret","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.insecure-random-secret","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-338: Use of Cryptographically Weak Pseudo-Random Number Generator (PRNG)","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.insecure-random-secret"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The RSA key is shorter than 2048 bits and can be factored with practical effort. Generate RSA keys of at least 3072 bits (2048 bits is the minimum accepted today), or use an elliptic-curve key."},"help":{"markdown":"The RSA key is shorter than 2048 bits and can be factored with practical effort. Generate RSA keys of at least 3072 bits (2048 bits is the minimum accepted today), or use an elliptic-curve key.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cryptography.io/en/latest/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/rsa/#generation](https://cryptography.io/en/latest/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/rsa/#generation)\n - [https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/SpecialPublications/NIST.SP.800-131Ar2.pdf](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/SpecialPublications/NIST.SP.800-131Ar2.pdf)\n","text":"The RSA key is shorter than 2048 bits and can be factored with practical effort. Generate RSA keys of at least 3072 bits (2048 bits is the minimum accepted today), or use an elliptic-curve key."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.small-rsa-key","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.small-rsa-key","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-326: Inadequate Encryption Strength","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.small-rsa-key"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The IV or nonce is a constant. Reusing an IV with the same key reveals relations between messages (CBC, CFB) and breaks confidentiality and integrity completely for CTR and GCM. Generate a new random IV for every message (os.urandom or secrets.token_bytes) and store it with the ciphertext."},"help":{"markdown":"The IV or nonce is a constant. Reusing an IV with the same key reveals relations between messages (CBC, CFB) and breaks confidentiality and integrity completely for CTR and GCM. Generate a new random IV for every message (os.urandom or secrets.token_bytes) and store it with the ciphertext.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cryptography.io/en/latest/hazmat/primitives/symmetric-encryption/#modes](https://cryptography.io/en/latest/hazmat/primitives/symmetric-encryption/#modes)\n","text":"The IV or nonce is a constant. Reusing an IV with the same key reveals relations between messages (CBC, CFB) and breaks confidentiality and integrity completely for CTR and GCM. Generate a new random IV for every message (os.urandom or secrets.token_bytes) and store it with the ciphertext."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.static-iv","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.static-iv","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-323: Reusing a Nonce, Key Pair in Encryption","CWE-329: Generation of Predictable IV with CBC Mode","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.static-iv"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"TLS certificate or host name verification is disabled. Any network attacker can then impersonate the server and read or change the traffic. Keep verification on and add a private CA to the trust store when needed."},"help":{"markdown":"TLS certificate or host name verification is disabled. Any network attacker can then impersonate the server and read or change the traffic. Keep verification on and add a private CA to the trust store when needed.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://docs.python.org/3/library/ssl.html#ssl.create_default_context](https://docs.python.org/3/library/ssl.html#ssl.create_default_context)\n - [https://www.python-httpx.org/advanced/ssl/](https://www.python-httpx.org/advanced/ssl/)\n","text":"TLS certificate or host name verification is disabled. Any network attacker can then impersonate the server and read or change the traffic. Keep verification on and add a private CA to the trust store when needed."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.tls-verification-disabled","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.tls-verification-disabled","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-295: Improper Certificate Validation","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.tls-verification-disabled"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A broken or obsolete cipher (DES, 3DES, RC4, RC2, Blowfish, CAST5, IDEA, SEED) is used. Their keys or block sizes are too small for current attacks; use AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305."},"help":{"markdown":"A broken or obsolete cipher (DES, 3DES, RC4, RC2, Blowfish, CAST5, IDEA, SEED) is used. Their keys or block sizes are too small for current attacks; use AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cryptography.io/en/latest/hazmat/decrepit/ciphers/](https://cryptography.io/en/latest/hazmat/decrepit/ciphers/)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html#algorithms](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html#algorithms)\n","text":"A broken or obsolete cipher (DES, 3DES, RC4, RC2, Blowfish, CAST5, IDEA, SEED) is used. Their keys or block sizes are too small for current attacks; use AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.weak-cipher","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.weak-cipher","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.weak-cipher"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"MD5 or SHA-1 is used. Both have practical collision attacks and must not protect integrity, signatures or passwords; use SHA-256 or better (and a password hash such as Argon2, scrypt or bcrypt for passwords). Pass usedforsecurity=False when the hash is not used for security."},"help":{"markdown":"MD5 or SHA-1 is used. Both have practical collision attacks and must not protect integrity, signatures or passwords; use SHA-256 or better (and a password hash such as Argon2, scrypt or bcrypt for passwords). Pass usedforsecurity=False when the hash is not used for security.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://docs.python.org/3/library/hashlib.html](https://docs.python.org/3/library/hashlib.html)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n","text":"MD5 or SHA-1 is used. Both have practical collision attacks and must not protect integrity, signatures or passwords; use SHA-256 or better (and a password hash such as Argon2, scrypt or bcrypt for passwords). Pass usedforsecurity=False when the hash is not used for security."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.weak-hash","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.weak-hash","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-328: Use of Weak Hash","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.crypto.python.weak-hash"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A database connection string contains a plaintext password. Anyone who can read the code or configuration can log in to the database, and the password cannot be rotated without a change. Read the credentials from a secrets manager or the environment and keep only placeholders in the repository."},"help":{"markdown":"A database connection string contains a plaintext password. Anyone who can read the code or configuration can log in to the database, and the password cannot be rotated without a change. Read the credentials from a secrets manager or the environment and keep only placeholders in the repository.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Database_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Database_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/798.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/798.html)\n","text":"A database connection string contains a plaintext password. Anyone who can read the code or configuration can log in to the database, and the password cannot be rotated without a change. Read the credentials from a secrets manager or the environment and keep only placeholders in the repository."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.connection-string-hardcoded-password","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.connection-string-hardcoded-password","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-259: Use of Hard-coded Password","CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.connection-string-hardcoded-password"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A database connection string turns TLS off or accepts any server certificate (sslmode=disable, useSSL=false, Encrypt=False, TrustServerCertificate=True, tlsInsecure=true and similar). Credentials and data then cross the network unprotected, or a network attacker can impersonate the database. Require TLS and verify the certificate (sslmode=verify-full, Encrypt=True)."},"help":{"markdown":"A database connection string turns TLS off or accepts any server certificate (sslmode=disable, useSSL=false, Encrypt=False, TrustServerCertificate=True, tlsInsecure=true and similar). Credentials and data then cross the network unprotected, or a network attacker can impersonate the database. Require TLS and verify the certificate (sslmode=verify-full, Encrypt=True).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/libpq-ssl.html#LIBPQ-SSL-PROTECTION](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/libpq-ssl.html#LIBPQ-SSL-PROTECTION)\n - [https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/connect/ado-net/connection-string-syntax](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/connect/ado-net/connection-string-syntax)\n","text":"A database connection string turns TLS off or accepts any server certificate (sslmode=disable, useSSL=false, Encrypt=False, TrustServerCertificate=True, tlsInsecure=true and similar). Credentials and data then cross the network unprotected, or a network attacker can impersonate the database. Require TLS and verify the certificate (sslmode=verify-full, Encrypt=True)."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.connection-string-tls-disabled","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.connection-string-tls-disabled","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-295: Improper Certificate Validation","CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.connection-string-tls-disabled"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An SQL statement is built with string concatenation, string.Format or an interpolated string and passed to ADO.NET (SqlCommand, CommandText) or Entity Framework (FromSqlRaw, ExecuteSqlRaw). Values that reach it can change the statement (SQL injection). Use SqlParameter or FromSql/FromSqlInterpolated."},"help":{"markdown":"An SQL statement is built with string concatenation, string.Format or an interpolated string and passed to ADO.NET (SqlCommand, CommandText) or Entity Framework (FromSqlRaw, ExecuteSqlRaw). Values that reach it can change the statement (SQL injection). Use SqlParameter or FromSql/FromSqlInterpolated.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/ef/core/querying/sql-queries#passing-parameters](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/ef/core/querying/sql-queries#passing-parameters)\n","text":"An SQL statement is built with string concatenation, string.Format or an interpolated string and passed to ADO.NET (SqlCommand, CommandText) or Entity Framework (FromSqlRaw, ExecuteSqlRaw). Values that reach it can change the statement (SQL injection). Use SqlParameter or FromSql/FromSqlInterpolated."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.csharp.sql-string-building","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.csharp.sql-string-building","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.csharp.sql-string-building"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A GORM raw SQL method (Raw, Exec, Where, Order, Select, Group, Having, Joins) receives a statement built with fmt.Sprintf or concatenation, which bypasses GORM's parameter binding (SQL injection). Pass values as arguments: db.Where(\"name = ?\", name)."},"help":{"markdown":"A GORM raw SQL method (Raw, Exec, Where, Order, Select, Group, Having, Joins) receives a statement built with fmt.Sprintf or concatenation, which bypasses GORM's parameter binding (SQL injection). Pass values as arguments: db.Where(\"name = ?\", name).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://gorm.io/docs/security.html](https://gorm.io/docs/security.html)\n","text":"A GORM raw SQL method (Raw, Exec, Where, Order, Select, Group, Having, Joins) receives a statement built with fmt.Sprintf or concatenation, which bypasses GORM's parameter binding (SQL injection). Pass values as arguments: db.Where(\"name = ?\", name)."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.go.gorm-raw-sql","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.go.gorm-raw-sql","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.go.gorm-raw-sql"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A MongoDB $where clause (server-side JavaScript) is built from a non-constant value. Values that reach it can run arbitrary JavaScript in the query (NoSQL injection). Use query operators instead."},"help":{"markdown":"A MongoDB $where clause (server-side JavaScript) is built from a non-constant value. Values that reach it can run arbitrary JavaScript in the query (NoSQL injection). Use query operators instead.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query/where/](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query/where/)\n","text":"A MongoDB $where clause (server-side JavaScript) is built from a non-constant value. Values that reach it can run arbitrary JavaScript in the query (NoSQL injection). Use query operators instead."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.go.nosql-injection","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.go.nosql-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-943: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Data Query Logic","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.go.nosql-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"HTTP request data (query string, form, path or header values) is concatenated into an SQL statement that is passed to database/sql, sqlx or pgx. The value can change the statement (SQL injection). Use placeholders ($1 or ?) and pass the value as an argument."},"help":{"markdown":"HTTP request data (query string, form, path or header values) is concatenated into an SQL statement that is passed to database/sql, sqlx or pgx. The value can change the statement (SQL injection). Use placeholders ($1 or ?) and pass the value as an argument.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://go.dev/doc/database/sql-injection](https://go.dev/doc/database/sql-injection)\n","text":"HTTP request data (query string, form, path or header values) is concatenated into an SQL statement that is passed to database/sql, sqlx or pgx. The value can change the statement (SQL injection). Use placeholders ($1 or ?) and pass the value as an argument."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.go.sql-string-concatenation","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.go.sql-string-concatenation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.go.sql-string-concatenation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An SQL statement is built with string concatenation or String.format and passed to JDBC (Statement, Connection.prepareStatement), JPA (createQuery, createNativeQuery) or Spring JdbcTemplate. Values that reach it can change the statement (SQL injection). Use a PreparedStatement with ? placeholders, or named parameters."},"help":{"markdown":"An SQL statement is built with string concatenation or String.format and passed to JDBC (Statement, Connection.prepareStatement), JPA (createQuery, createNativeQuery) or Spring JdbcTemplate. Values that reach it can change the statement (SQL injection). Use a PreparedStatement with ? placeholders, or named parameters.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/jdbc/basics/prepared.html](https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/jdbc/basics/prepared.html)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Query_Parameterization_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Query_Parameterization_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n","text":"An SQL statement is built with string concatenation or String.format and passed to JDBC (Statement, Connection.prepareStatement), JPA (createQuery, createNativeQuery) or Spring JdbcTemplate. Values that reach it can change the statement (SQL injection). Use a PreparedStatement with ? placeholders, or named parameters."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.java.jdbc-string-building","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.java.jdbc-string-building","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.java.jdbc-string-building"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A MongoDB $where clause (server-side JavaScript) is built from a non-constant value. Values that reach it can run arbitrary JavaScript in the query (NoSQL injection). Use query operators (Filters.eq and similar)."},"help":{"markdown":"A MongoDB $where clause (server-side JavaScript) is built from a non-constant value. Values that reach it can run arbitrary JavaScript in the query (NoSQL injection). Use query operators (Filters.eq and similar).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query/where/](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query/where/)\n","text":"A MongoDB $where clause (server-side JavaScript) is built from a non-constant value. Values that reach it can run arbitrary JavaScript in the query (NoSQL injection). Use query operators (Filters.eq and similar)."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.java.nosql-injection","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.java.nosql-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-943: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Data Query Logic","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.java.nosql-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A request value (req.body, req.query, req.params) is used as a MongoDB query value without conversion. A JSON body or a query string such as user[$ne]=x can carry query operators instead of plain values and change what the query matches (NoSQL injection). Convert values with String() or validate them; with Mongoose, keep sanitizeFilter enabled."},"help":{"markdown":"A request value (req.body, req.query, req.params) is used as a MongoDB query value without conversion. A JSON body or a query string such as user[$ne]=x can carry query operators instead of plain values and change what the query matches (NoSQL injection). Convert values with String() or validate them; with Mongoose, keep sanitizeFilter enabled.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/latest/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/07-Input_Validation_Testing/05.6-Testing_for_NoSQL_Injection](https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/latest/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/07-Input_Validation_Testing/05.6-Testing_for_NoSQL_Injection)\n - [https://mongoosejs.com/docs/api/mongoose.html#Mongoose.prototype.sanitizeFilter()](https://mongoosejs.com/docs/api/mongoose.html#Mongoose.prototype.sanitizeFilter())\n","text":"A request value (req.body, req.query, req.params) is used as a MongoDB query value without conversion. A JSON body or a query string such as user[$ne]=x can carry query operators instead of plain values and change what the query matches (NoSQL injection). Convert values with String() or validate them; with Mongoose, keep sanitizeFilter enabled."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.javascript.nosql-injection","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.javascript.nosql-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-943: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Data Query Logic","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.javascript.nosql-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Sequelize.literal() inserts its argument into the SQL statement unescaped; here the argument is not a constant (SQL injection). Use replacements or bind parameters, or Sequelize.escape() for single values."},"help":{"markdown":"Sequelize.literal() inserts its argument into the SQL statement unescaped; here the argument is not a constant (SQL injection). Use replacements or bind parameters, or Sequelize.escape() for single values.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://sequelize.org/api/v6/class/src/sequelize.js~sequelize#static-method-literal](https://sequelize.org/api/v6/class/src/sequelize.js~sequelize#static-method-literal)\n - [https://sequelize.org/docs/v6/core-concepts/raw-queries/#replacements](https://sequelize.org/docs/v6/core-concepts/raw-queries/#replacements)\n","text":"Sequelize.literal() inserts its argument into the SQL statement unescaped; here the argument is not a constant (SQL injection). Use replacements or bind parameters, or Sequelize.escape() for single values."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.javascript.sequelize-literal","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.javascript.sequelize-literal","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.javascript.sequelize-literal"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An SQL statement is built with string concatenation or a template literal and passed to a database client (mysql, pg, mssql, sqlite, Sequelize, TypeORM, knex). Values that reach it can change the statement (SQL injection). Use placeholders and pass the values separately."},"help":{"markdown":"An SQL statement is built with string concatenation or a template literal and passed to a database client (mysql, pg, mssql, sqlite, Sequelize, TypeORM, knex). Values that reach it can change the statement (SQL injection). Use placeholders and pass the values separately.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Query_Parameterization_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Query_Parameterization_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://node-postgres.com/features/queries#parameterized-query](https://node-postgres.com/features/queries#parameterized-query)\n","text":"An SQL statement is built with string concatenation or a template literal and passed to a database client (mysql, pg, mssql, sqlite, Sequelize, TypeORM, knex). Values that reach it can change the statement (SQL injection). Use placeholders and pass the values separately."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.javascript.sql-string-building","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.javascript.sql-string-building","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.javascript.sql-string-building"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Django raw SQL (Manager.raw, QuerySet.extra or RawSQL) receives a statement built with string formatting or concatenation, which bypasses the ORM's escaping (SQL injection). Pass values in params=[...] and keep the statement a constant."},"help":{"markdown":"Django raw SQL (Manager.raw, QuerySet.extra or RawSQL) receives a statement built with string formatting or concatenation, which bypasses the ORM's escaping (SQL injection). Pass values in params=[...] and keep the statement a constant.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/topics/db/sql/](https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/topics/db/sql/)\n - [https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/ref/models/querysets/#extra](https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/ref/models/querysets/#extra)\n","text":"Django raw SQL (Manager.raw, QuerySet.extra or RawSQL) receives a statement built with string formatting or concatenation, which bypasses the ORM's escaping (SQL injection). Pass values in params=[...] and keep the statement a constant."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.python.django-raw-sql","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.python.django-raw-sql","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.python.django-raw-sql"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Request data reaches a MongoDB query without validation. A JSON body can carry query operators ($ne, $gt, $regex, $where) instead of plain values and change what the query matches, for example to bypass a log-in check (NoSQL injection). Convert values to the expected type (str(), int()) or validate them with a schema."},"help":{"markdown":"Request data reaches a MongoDB query without validation. A JSON body can carry query operators ($ne, $gt, $regex, $where) instead of plain values and change what the query matches, for example to bypass a log-in check (NoSQL injection). Convert values to the expected type (str(), int()) or validate them with a schema.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/latest/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/07-Input_Validation_Testing/05.6-Testing_for_NoSQL_Injection](https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/latest/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/07-Input_Validation_Testing/05.6-Testing_for_NoSQL_Injection)\n","text":"Request data reaches a MongoDB query without validation. A JSON body can carry query operators ($ne, $gt, $regex, $where) instead of plain values and change what the query matches, for example to bypass a log-in check (NoSQL injection). Convert values to the expected type (str(), int()) or validate them with a schema."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.python.nosql-injection","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.python.nosql-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-943: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Data Query Logic","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.python.nosql-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An SQL statement is built with string concatenation, %-formatting, str.format or an f-string and passed to a DB-API cursor. Values that reach it can change the statement (SQL injection). Pass them as query parameters: cursor.execute(\"SELECT ... WHERE id = %s\", (value,))."},"help":{"markdown":"An SQL statement is built with string concatenation, %-formatting, str.format or an f-string and passed to a DB-API cursor. Values that reach it can change the statement (SQL injection). Pass them as query parameters: cursor.execute(\"SELECT ... WHERE id = %s\", (value,)).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://peps.python.org/pep-0249/#id15](https://peps.python.org/pep-0249/#id15)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Query_Parameterization_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Query_Parameterization_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n","text":"An SQL statement is built with string concatenation, %-formatting, str.format or an f-string and passed to a DB-API cursor. Values that reach it can change the statement (SQL injection). Pass them as query parameters: cursor.execute(\"SELECT ... WHERE id = %s\", (value,))."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.python.sql-string-building","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.python.sql-string-building","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.python.sql-string-building"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"sqlalchemy.text() receives a statement built with string formatting or concatenation, so values become SQL (SQL injection). Use bound parameters: text(\"... WHERE id = :id\") with execute(stmt, {\"id\": value})."},"help":{"markdown":"sqlalchemy.text() receives a statement built with string formatting or concatenation, so values become SQL (SQL injection). Use bound parameters: text(\"... WHERE id = :id\") with execute(stmt, {\"id\": value}).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/20/core/sqlelement.html#sqlalchemy.sql.expression.text](https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/20/core/sqlelement.html#sqlalchemy.sql.expression.text)\n","text":"sqlalchemy.text() receives a statement built with string formatting or concatenation, so values become SQL (SQL injection). Use bound parameters: text(\"... WHERE id = :id\") with execute(stmt, {\"id\": value})."},"id":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.python.sqlalchemy-text-formatting","name":"opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.python.sqlalchemy-text-formatting","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: opt.pathos.rules.pathos.database.python.sqlalchemy-text-formatting"}}],"semanticVersion":"2.0.0"}}}],"$schema":"https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json"}
